<div class="path-head"><p class="featured-region">Reading path · 8 stops</p><h1 class="path-title">The Crusades</h1><p class="path-tagline">Two centuries of holy war for the eastern Mediterranean, and the states it built and broke.</p><p class="path-intro">In 1095 a pope's sermon set armed pilgrims marching east, and for two hundred years Latin Christendom fought for Jerusalem and the coast of the Levant. The crusades planted fragile kingdoms in the East, bled Byzantium, raised up Saladin and the sultans who answered the call to jihad, and bound Europe to the Mediterranean world it had half-forgotten. This path follows the whole arc, from Clermont to the fall of the crusader states.</p><p class="path-types">Suits <a href="/start">the Strategist</a> · <a href="/start">the Chronicler</a></p></div>
<ol class="path-steps"><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/pope-urban-ii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-urban-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">1 · Encyclopedia · Person · c. 1035–1099</span><span class="path-step-name">Pope Urban II</span><span class="path-step-why">The pope whose sermon at Clermont in 1095 launched the First Crusade.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-crusade.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">2 · Encyclopedia · Event · captured Jerusalem 1099</span><span class="path-step-name">First Crusade</span><span class="path-step-why">Against every expectation, the first expedition took Jerusalem in 1099 and made the crusading idea seem blessed.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/empire/kingdom-of-jerusalem"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/church-of-the-holy-sepulchre.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">3 · Profile · 1099 CE – 1291 CE</span><span class="path-step-name">Kingdom of Jerusalem</span><span class="path-step-why">The greatest of the crusader states: how a conquered coast was ruled, defended and finally lost.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/saladin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saladin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">4 · Encyclopedia · Person · d. 1193</span><span class="path-step-name">Saladin</span><span class="path-step-why">The Kurdish sultan who united Egypt and Syria and turned the tide of the holy war.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hattin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-hattin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">5 · Encyclopedia · Event · 1187</span><span class="path-step-name">Battle of Hattin</span><span class="path-step-why">One July day in 1187 destroyed the kingdom's army and gave Jerusalem back to Islam.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/krak-des-chevaliers"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/krak-des-chevaliers.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">6 · Encyclopedia · Work</span><span class="path-step-name">Krak des Chevaliers</span><span class="path-step-why">The greatest of the crusader castles, and what fortress architecture reveals about holding hostile land.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">7 · Encyclopedia · Event · 1204</span><span class="path-step-name">Fourth Crusade</span><span class="path-step-why">The crusade that never reached Jerusalem: it sacked Christian Constantinople instead, and Byzantium never fully recovered.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/crusader-states.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">8 · Encyclopedia · State</span><span class="path-step-name">Crusader states</span><span class="path-step-why">The settlements as a whole - Edessa, Antioch, Tripoli, Jerusalem - and why they could not last.</span></span></a></li></ol>
